      "title": "6105 Six-Month Shaving Accommodation (Officer)",
      "description": "Six-month 6105 counseling for a Marine officer on a clean-shaven medical accommodation under MCO 1020.34H (the counseling MARADMIN 348/26 para 3.b.3.a requires; wording per MARADMIN 192/26).",
      "documentType": "page11"
    }
  },
  "data": {
    "formData": {
      "documentType": "page11",
      "name": "",
      "edipi": "",
      "date": "",
      "remarksLeft": "[YYYYMMDD]: Counseled this date concerning the following deficiencies: inability to comply with clean-shaven grooming standards established in MCO 1020.34H, having reached six total months of continuous treatment requiring a medical accommodation.\n\nThe accommodation was approved by the commanding officer on [YYYYMMDD] and documented on NAVMC 11830. The accommodation expires [YYYYMMDD], twelve months from the date of approval. Marines who require clean-shaven grooming accommodations due to a medical condition for more than twelve months will be evaluated for continued service and may be considered for the initiation of separation proceeding if the medical condition has not improved, is not classified as a disability, and adversely affects good order and discipline.\n\nSpecific recommendations for corrective action are to comply fully with the prescribed medical treatment plan, to attend all scheduled medical evaluations and re-evaluations as appropriate, to obtain an administrative extension prior to expiration of my accommodation. To retain a copy of my approved medical accommodation in my possession in either hard copy or digital format and present it to leadership upon request. To seek assistance, which is available through the chain of command and the unit Independent Duty Corpsman or Medical Officer.\n\nGrooming Standards: You must strictly maintain facial hair length not to exceed one quarter of an inch (0.25) in length.\n\nYou will be required to be clean-shaven when deployed to environments with a high threat of chemical, biological, radiological, and nuclear (CBRN) attack, in receipt of hostile fire pay or imminent danger pay, when deployed, or when conducting CBRN training requiring the wear of a field protective mask.\n\nFailure to take corrective action and any further violations of the UCMJ, disciplinary action, or incidents requiring formal counseling may result in judicial or adverse administrative action, including but not limited to administrative separation. I understand that failure to complete my enlistment contract with an honorable characterization of service may preclude my eligibility for benefits from the Department of Veterans Affairs or other organizations and have an adverse effect on future civilian employment.\n\nI was advised that within 5 working days after acknowledging this entry I may submit a written rebuttal which will be filed in my official military personnel file (OMPF).\n\nI choose to ____ / not to ____ make such a statement.\n\n\n_____________________          _____________________\nSignature of Marine Officer    Signature of Commanding Officer",
      "remarksRight": ""
    },
